<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  What the hardened runtime lets this app do, and nothing else.

  Four keys, and each is here because something breaks without it:

  - `com.apple.security.device.audio-input` — the microphone. Without it a
    hardened-runtime build is refused by TCC before a dialog is ever shown, so
    the app appears to record and captures silence. It is also half of what
    ScreenCaptureKit's system-audio tap needs; the other half is Screen
    Recording, which is a TCC grant rather than an entitlement and cannot be
    declared here.
  - `com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit` and
    `com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory` — Chromium's V8.
    Every Electron app needs both under the hardened runtime; without them the
    renderer crashes at launch.
  - `com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation` — Electron's own helper
    binaries and any native module load into the app's process. Without it a
    signed app refuses its own framework.

  Deliberately NOT here, and each absence is a decision:

  - `com.apple.security.device.camera`. This app has no video path at all. The
    `getDisplayMedia` call takes a video track because the API requires one and
    stops it before a frame is read.
  - `com.apple.security.network.server`. The loopback listener that receives the
    OAuth redirect binds 127.0.0.1 in the main process, which is not sandboxed
    and needs no entitlement for it. Adding one would be asking for a permission
    to do something already permitted.
  - `com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write`. Nothing here opens a
    file the person chose. Notes go to the bucket, not to disk.
  - The App Sandbox itself. Notarised distribution outside the Mac App Store
    does not require it, and the app reads process lists and drives Calendar
    over JXA — both of which the sandbox forbids. If this ever goes to the Mac
    App Store, that is a different build with a different detection story, and
    it is a decision rather than a flag.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
